  "conservation_statement": "Textiles are light sensitive, and damage to textiles from overexposure to light is cumulative and irreversible. One of the signs of light damage in textiles is the fading of dyes. In the case of this embroidered textile, by comparing the silk embroidery colors on the front to those on the back that have been protected from light, we know the silk embroidery colors have faded to more muted tones.",
